I come out of the room.
The opposite door opens.
There is a woman there.
There is a small dog with her.
The woman smiles.
"Hello," she says.
"Hello," I say.
"My name is Asha," she says.
"And this is my dog, Moti."
"Are you new here?" she asks.
"Yes, I am new," I say.
"My name is Maya."
"I am from Mexico."
"Oh wow!" Asha says.
"Do you need anything?" she asks.
"No, thank you," I say.
"Everything is fine."
"Okay."
"Good night, Maya," she says.
"Good night, Asha," I say.
She and Moti go outside.
